{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Hagar, Sarai's maidservant.</b> We already know that she was Sarai's maidservant, for it was mentioned above — 'and she had an Egyptian maidservant whose name was Hagar.'" "<b>But.</b> It is possible to explain that the angel mentioned 'Sarai's maidservant' for two reasons: the first, to indicate that the angel's speech did not come to this Egyptian woman except for the honor that she was Sarai's maidservant. And the second, to establish the status of bondwoman and servitude, that she should be subservient to Sarai all her days, as he said to her, ״return to your mistress״ and so on; and also her seed are destined to be subservient to Sarah's seed at the end of days."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:46.087445003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}